> Keep the final observation when auto-resetting

Two CartPoles with limit1 truncate after their first safe step. Each vector row returns both the old episode final observation and the new episode reset observation. These have the same width but different meanings.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vec_env_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace e=dm::rl::environments;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");e::VecEnv env([]{return std::make_unique<e::CartPole>(1);},2,1,2);env.reset();auto r=env.step({0,1});std::vector<double>values;for(int i=0;i<2;++i){if(!r.truncated[i]||r.final_obs[i].size()!=4||r.obs[i].size()!=4)return 1;values.push_back(r.final_obs[i][0]);values.push_back(r.obs[i][0]);}std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);dm::nn::save_npz("build/vec_env_worked.npz",{{"values",dm::nn::from_vector(values)}});std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);const double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1e-9,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).bars(x,values,"computed values",{37,99,235}).title("Keep the final observation when auto-resetting").x_label("Coordinate in displayed calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/vec_env_worked.svg");}
```
