> Track auto-reset boundaries explicitly

Four seeded CartPoles with a five-step limit expose cumulative done counts. Auto-reset observations belong to the next episode; saved final observations belong to the episode that just ended. Two worker threads execute this diagnostic.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vec_env_boundaries.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace e=dm::rl::environments;e::VecEnv env([]{return std::make_unique<e::CartPole>(5);},4,1,2);env.reset();std::vector<double>step,finished;int total=0;for(int t=0;t<20;++t){auto result=env.step({0,1,0,1});for(int i=0;i<4;++i)if(result.done(i)){++total;if(result.final_obs[i].size()!=4)return 1;}step.push_back(t+1);finished.push_back(total);}dm::nn::save_npz("build/vec_env_boundaries.npz",{{"step",dm::nn::from_vector(step)},{"finished",dm::nn::from_vector(finished)}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().lines(step,finished,"ended episodes",{37,99,235}).x_label("Vector step").y_label("Cumulative ended episodes").title("Final-observation and auto-reset boundaries").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/vec_env_boundaries.svg");}
```
